IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV, Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums:
-- section 81 (interpretation) and sections 82 to 84 (deducting and remitting premiums, what follows a failure to do so,
-- directors' liability, and the employer's premium not being recoverable from the insured person).
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as plain inputs (see NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my ranges"):
--   * "the prescribed amount", "the prescribed time", "the prescribed manner", "a prescribed person", "the prescribed rate":
--     the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations (SOR/97-33), which are not among the inputs;
--   * the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year: the keel's s 4 gives the formula, the published figure is an input;
--   * the Income Tax Act (not deposited): "financial institution" in s 190(1), and ss 227.1(2) to (7) in s 83(2);
--   * rulings and appeals under ss 90, 91 and 103 (this piece, other modules): their outcomes are facts here.
-- "Employer" is the keel's `s 2(1) employer`; "insured person" is the keel's `s 2(1) insured person`; each is a BOOLEAN input.

§ `Section 81 - Part IV interpretation`

-- src:1299 | authorized person means a person authorized by the Minister for the purposes of this Part; (personne autorisée)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 81 "authorized person" (src:1299)
GIVEN `is a person authorized by the Minister for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 81 authorized person` IF
    `is a person authorized by the Minister for the purposes of this Part`

-- src:1300 | judge means a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises or a judge of the Federal Court; (juge)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 81 "judge" (src:1300)
GIVEN `is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a judge of the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 81 judge` IF
        `is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises`
    OR  `is a judge of the Federal Court`

-- "Minister" in Part IV is the Minister of National Revenue (s 81, src:1301); the keel's `s 2(1) the Minister for`
-- already answers it for `Part IV`, so this module encodes nothing more for that definition.

§ `Section 82(1) to (3.1) - deduction and remittance`

-- Subsection (2): "have reached" is read as AT LEAST the maximum, on the earnings paid BEFORE the payment now being made
-- (fork F-ei3-9). The maximum is the year's published figure (an input; the keel gives s 4's formula).
-- src:1309 | (2) The employer shall not make any deduction as or on account of the person’s premium for a year if in that year the insurable earnings paid by the employer to the person have reached the maximum yearly insurable earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(2) (src:1309)
GIVEN `the insurable earnings paid by the employer to the person in the year, before this payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(2) the employer shall not make any deduction for the year` IF
    `the insurable earnings paid by the employer to the person in the year, before this payment`
        AT LEAST `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`

-- src:1305 | 82 (1) Every employer paying remuneration to a person they employ in insurable employment shall
-- src:1306 | (a) deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration as or on account of the employee’s premium payable by that insured person under section 67 for any period for which the remuneration is paid; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(1)(a), s 82(2) (src:1305-1306) (src:1309)
GIVEN `pays remuneration to a person they employ in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurable earnings paid by the employer to the person in the year, before this payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(1)(a) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration` IF
        `pays remuneration to a person they employ in insurable employment`
    AND (NOT `s 82(2) the employer shall not make any deduction for the year` `the insurable earnings paid by the employer to the person in the year, before this payment` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`)

-- Paragraph (b): the amount deducted, together with the employer's premium for that period (s 68), to the Receiver General
-- at the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner. "Remit the amount, together with the employer's premium": at least
-- both amounts, on or before the prescribed day, in the prescribed manner.
-- src:1307 | (b) remit the amount, together with the employer’s premium payable by the employer under section 68 for that period, to the Receiver General at the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(1)(b) (src:1307)
GIVEN `the amount deducted as the employee's premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the employer's premium payable for that period` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount remitted to the Receiver General` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which it was remitted` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed time by which it had to be remitted` IS A DATE
      `it was remitted in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(1)(b) the employer has remitted as the paragraph requires` IF
        `the amount remitted to the Receiver General` AT LEAST (`the amount deducted as the employee's premium` PLUS `the employer's premium payable for that period`)
    AND `the day on which it was remitted` AT MOST `the prescribed time by which it had to be remitted`
    AND `it was remitted in the prescribed manner`

-- Subsection (3): a prescribed person (at the prescribed time) remits to the account of the Receiver General at a
-- financial institution (the Income Tax Act's meaning, read without paragraphs (d) and (e) of s 190(1); not deposited).
-- src:1311 | (3) If the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time, the remittance shall be made to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution, within the meaning that would be assigned by the definition financial institution in subsection 190(1) of the Income Tax Act if it were read without reference to paragraphs (d) and (e) of that subsection.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(3) (src:1311)
GIVEN `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the remittance was made to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution as described in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(3) the remittance was made as the subsection requires` IF
        (NOT `the employer is a prescribed person at the prescribed time`)
    OR  `the remittance was made to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution as described in subsection (3)`

-- Subsection (3.1): deemed remitted to the financial institution if remitted to the Receiver General "at least one day
-- before the day on which the amount is due".
-- src:1313 | (3.1) For the purpose of subsection (3), a prescribed person referred to in that subsection is deemed to have remitted an amount to the account of the Receiver General at a financial institution referred to in that subsection if the prescribed person has remitted the amount to the Receiver General at least one day before the day on which the amount is due.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(3.1) (src:1313)
GIVEN `the person is a prescribed person referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person remitted the amount to the Receiver General` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the amount is due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(3.1) the prescribed person is deemed to have remitted the amount to the account at a financial institution` IF
        `the person is a prescribed person referred to in subsection (3)`
    AND (`the day on which the person remitted the amount to the Receiver General` PLUS 1) AT MOST `the day on which the amount is due`

§ `Section 82(4) to (7) - failure to deduct`

-- Subsection (5): not liable if (a) informed in writing, in a ruling under s 90, that no deduction was required, (b) the ruling
-- was not based on material incorrect information given by the employer, and (c) it is later decided under s 91 or 103
-- that the deduction should have been made.
-- src:1317 | (5) An employer is not liable for failing to make a deduction from the remuneration of an insured person or for any amount that should have been deducted if
-- src:1318 | (a) the employer is informed in writing in a ruling under section 90 that the employer is not required to make the deduction,
-- src:1319 | (b) the ruling is not based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular, and
-- src:1320 | (c) it is subsequently decided under section 91 or 103 that the deduction should have been made,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(5) (src:1317-1320)
GIVEN `the employer was informed in writing in a ruling under section 90 that the employer is not required to make the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ruling was based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was subsequently decided under section 91 or 103 that the deduction should have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(5) the employer is not liable for failing to make the deduction` IF
        `the employer was informed in writing in a ruling under section 90 that the employer is not required to make the deduction`
    AND (NOT `the ruling was based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular`)
    AND `it was subsequently decided under section 91 or 103 that the deduction should have been made`

-- "Once the decision under section 91 or 103 is communicated to the employer, the employer is liable without interest or
-- penalties under this Act to pay the premium required to be paid by the employer with respect to the insured person."
-- src:1317 | (5) An employer is not liable for failing to make a deduction from the remuneration of an insured person or for any amount that should have been deducted if
-- src:1318 | (a) the employer is informed in writing in a ruling under section 90 that the employer is not required to make the deduction,
-- src:1319 | (b) the ruling is not based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular, and
-- src:1320 | (c) it is subsequently decided under section 91 or 103 that the deduction should have been made,
-- src:1321 | but once the decision under section 91 or 103 is communicated to the employer, the employer is liable without interest or penalties under this Act to pay the premium required to be paid by the employer with respect to the insured person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(5) (src:1317-1321)
GIVEN `the employer was informed in writing in a ruling under section 90 that the employer is not required to make the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ruling was based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was subsequently decided under section 91 or 103 that the deduction should have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision has been communicated to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(5) the employer is liable, without interest or penalties, to pay the employer's premium` IF
        `s 82(5) the employer is not liable for failing to make the deduction` `the employer was informed in writing in a ruling under section 90 that the employer is not required to make the deduction` `the ruling was based on information provided by the employer to the Minister that was incorrect in a material particular` `it was subsequently decided under section 91 or 103 that the deduction should have been made`
    AND `the decision has been communicated to the employer`

-- Subsection (4): "Subject to subsection (5)": liable for the whole amount that should have been deducted and remitted,
-- from the time it should have been deducted.
-- src:1315 | (4) Subject to subsection (5), an employer who fails to deduct and remit an amount from the remuneration of an insured person as and when required under subsection (1) is liable to pay to Her Majesty the whole amount that should have been deducted and remitted from the time it should have been deducted.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(4) (src:1315)
GIVEN `fails to deduct and remit an amount from the remuneration of an insured person as and when required under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 82(5) applies to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(4) the employer is liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount` IF
        `fails to deduct and remit an amount from the remuneration of an insured person as and when required under subsection (1)`
    AND (NOT `s 82(5) applies to the employer`)

-- Subsection (6): the employer may deduct a premium it failed to deduct from "any subsequent payment of remuneration made
-- within 12 months after making the payment from which the deduction was required", but not, in addition to the premium
-- required by (1), more than one other premium it previously failed to deduct.
-- src:1323 | (6) An employer who fails to deduct the employee’s premium as required by subsection (1) from a payment of remuneration to an insured person may deduct an amount equal to it from any subsequent payment of remuneration made to the insured person within 12 months after making the payment from which the deduction was required, but the employer may not deduct, in addition to the premium required by subsection (1), more than one other such premium that the employer previously failed to deduct.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(6) (src:1323)
GIVEN `the day on which the payment from which the deduction was required was made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the subsequent payment of remuneration is made` IS A DATE
      `the number of other premiums the employer previously failed to deduct that it also deducts from the subsequent payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` IF
        `the day on which the subsequent payment of remuneration is made` GREATER THAN `the day on which the payment from which the deduction was required was made`
    AND `the day on which the subsequent payment of remuneration is made` AT MOST (`add months` `the day on which the payment from which the deduction was required was made` 12)
    AND `the number of other premiums the employer previously failed to deduct that it also deducts from the subsequent payment` AT MOST 1

-- Subsection (7): an amount deducted under (1) is deemed received, at that time, by the insured person.
-- src:1325 | (7) If an amount has been deducted under subsection (1), it is deemed for all purposes to have been received at that time by the insured person to whom the remuneration was payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(7) (src:1325)
GIVEN `an amount has been deducted under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which it was deducted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 82(7) the day on which the insured person is deemed to have received the amount` IS
    IF `an amount has been deducted under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST `the day on which it was deducted`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 82(8) and (9) - interest and penalty on amounts not remitted`

-- Subsection (8): interest at the prescribed rate "computed from the day on which the employer was so required to remit the
-- amount to the day of remittance". The rate and the method of computing are prescribed (not among the inputs), so the
-- encoding gives the duty and the period, not the interest in dollars (see NOTES.md, "What the text turns out to say").
-- src:1327 | (8) If an employer has failed to remit to the Receiver General an amount that the employer was required to remit at the time when it was required, the employer shall pay to the Receiver General interest on that amount at the prescribed rate computed from the day on which the employer was so required to remit the amount to the day of remittance of the amount to the Receiver General.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(8) (src:1327)
GIVEN `the employer failed to remit the amount at the time when it was required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(8) the employer shall pay interest to the Receiver General` IF
    `the employer failed to remit the amount at the time when it was required`

-- src:1327 | (8) If an employer has failed to remit to the Receiver General an amount that the employer was required to remit at the time when it was required, the employer shall pay to the Receiver General interest on that amount at the prescribed rate computed from the day on which the employer was so required to remit the amount to the day of remittance of the amount to the Receiver General.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(8) (src:1327)
GIVEN `the day on which the employer was required to remit the amount` IS A DATE
      `the day of remittance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 82(8) the period for which interest is computed` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the day on which the employer was required to remit the amount`, `the day of remittance`

-- Subsection (9): the rate of the penalty. NOTHING means no penalty: the amount was received by the due day AND paid in the
-- manner required, so there was no failure to remit. Days are counted from the day the amount was due (0 is that day).
-- Paragraph (b) (20%) prevails over (a) ("subject to paragraph (b)"). Paragraph (a)(iii) covers both an amount received
-- after the seventh day and an amount never received (NOTHING days).
-- src:1329 | (9) Every employer who in a year fails to remit to the Receiver General an amount that the employer is required to remit at the time when it is required is liable to a penalty of
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(9) (src:1329)
GIVEN `days after the due day when received, if received` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount was paid in the manner required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(9) there was a failure to remit` IS
    CONSIDER `days after the due day when received, if received`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST late THEN (late GREATER THAN 0) OR (NOT `the amount was paid in the manner required`)

-- src:1330 | (a) subject to paragraph (b), if
-- src:1331 | (i) the Receiver General receives that amount on or before the day it was due, but that amount is not paid in the manner required, 3% of that amount,
-- src:1332 | (ii) the Receiver General receives that amount
-- src:1333 | (A) no more than three days after it was due, 3% of that amount,
-- src:1334 | (B) more than three days and no more than five days after it was due, 5% of that amount, or
-- src:1335 | (C) more than five days and no more than seven days after it was due, 7% of that amount, or
-- src:1336 | (iii) that amount is not paid or remitted on or before the seventh day after it was due, 10% of that amount; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(9)(a) (src:1330-1336)
GIVEN `days after the due day when received, if received` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` IS
    CONSIDER `days after the due day when received, if received`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 10%
    WHEN JUST late THEN
        BRANCH IF late AT MOST 0 THEN 3%
               IF late AT MOST 3 THEN 3%
               IF late AT MOST 5 THEN 5%
               IF late AT MOST 7 THEN 7%
               OTHERWISE 10%

-- src:1329 | (9) Every employer who in a year fails to remit to the Receiver General an amount that the employer is required to remit at the time when it is required is liable to a penalty of
-- src:1330 | (a) subject to paragraph (b), if
-- src:1331 | (i) the Receiver General receives that amount on or before the day it was due, but that amount is not paid in the manner required, 3% of that amount,
-- src:1332 | (ii) the Receiver General receives that amount
-- src:1333 | (A) no more than three days after it was due, 3% of that amount,
-- src:1334 | (B) more than three days and no more than five days after it was due, 5% of that amount, or
-- src:1335 | (C) more than five days and no more than seven days after it was due, 7% of that amount, or
-- src:1336 | (iii) that amount is not paid or remitted on or before the seventh day after it was due, 10% of that amount; or
-- src:1337 | (b) 20% of the amount if at the time of the failure a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer for an amount that the employer was required to remit during the year and the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(9) (src:1329-1337)
GIVEN `days after the due day when received, if received` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount was paid in the manner required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the failure a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer for an amount required to be remitted during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` IS
    IF (NOT `s 82(9) there was a failure to remit` `days after the due day when received, if received` `the amount was paid in the manner required`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `at the time of the failure a penalty under this subsection was payable by the employer for an amount required to be remitted during the year`
            AND `the failure was made knowingly or under circumstances amounting to gross negligence`
         THEN JUST (20%)
         ELSE JUST (`s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` `days after the due day when received, if received`)

-- src:1329 | (9) Every employer who in a year fails to remit to the Receiver General an amount that the employer is required to remit at the time when it is required is liable to a penalty of
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82(9) (src:1329)
GIVEN `the amount that the employer was required to remit` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate of the penalty` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 82(9) the penalty in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `the rate of the penalty`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (rate TIMES `the amount that the employer was required to remit`)

§ `Section 82.01 - excess payment deemed not deducted`

-- The conditions of subsection (1): a year after 2015; the excess paid as remuneration to an insured person by a clerical,
-- administrative or system error; by the end of the third year after the calendar year of the deduction (a) the employer
-- elected AND (b) the insured person repaid or arranged to repay; no correcting return filed before the election; any
-- additional conditions the Minister specified are met. "Before the end of the third year": up to and including 31 December
-- of that year (fork F-ei3-10).
-- src:1339 | 82.01 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an amount deducted by an employer under subsection 82(1) for a year after 2015 in respect of an excess payment that was paid — as a result of a clerical, administrative or system error — as remuneration to an insured person is deemed not to have been deducted for the purposes of this Act if
-- src:1340 | (a) before the end of the third year after the calendar year in which the amount was deducted,
-- src:1341 | (i) the employer elects to have this section apply in respect of the amount, and
-- src:1342 | (ii) the insured person has repaid, or made an arrangement to repay, the employer;
-- src:1343 | (b) the employer has not filed an information return correcting for the excess payment before making the election referred to in subparagraph (a)(i); and
-- src:1344 | (c) any additional conditions specified by the Minister are met.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82.01(1) (src:1339-1344)
GIVEN `the year for which the amount was deducted` IS A NUMBER
      `the calendar year in which the amount was deducted` IS A NUMBER
      `the excess payment was paid as remuneration to an insured person as a result of a clerical, administrative or system error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the employer elected to have this section apply` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the insured person repaid, or made an arrangement to repay, the employer, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the employer filed an information return correcting for the excess payment before making the election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any additional conditions specified by the Minister are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` IF
        `the year for which the amount was deducted` GREATER THAN 2015
    AND `the excess payment was paid as remuneration to an insured person as a result of a clerical, administrative or system error`
    AND `the day on which the employer elected to have this section apply` AT MOST (`add years` (YMD `the calendar year in which the amount was deducted` 12 31) 3)
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the insured person repaid, or made an arrangement to repay, the employer, if they did`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST repaidOn THEN repaidOn AT MOST (`add years` (YMD `the calendar year in which the amount was deducted` 12 31) 3))
    AND (NOT `the employer filed an information return correcting for the excess payment before making the election`)
    AND `any additional conditions specified by the Minister are met`

-- Subsection (2): the amount deemed not deducted is the amount deducted, or if A minus B is less than that, A minus B.
-- src:1346 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the amount that is deemed not to have been deducted is the amount that was deducted by the employer or, if the amount determined by the following formula is less than the amount that was deducted by the employer, the amount determined by the formula
-- src:1347 | A − B
-- src:1348 | where
-- src:1349 | A is the aggregate of all amounts that were deducted by the employer as the employee’s premiums for the year in question; and
-- src:1350 | B is the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted by the employer as the employee’s premiums for that year had the employer not made the excess payment referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82.01(2) (src:1346-1350)
GIVEN `the amount that was deducted by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `A, the aggregate of all amounts deducted by the employer as the employee's premiums for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted had the employer not made the excess payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 82.01(2) the amount deemed not to have been deducted` IS
    IF (`A, the aggregate of all amounts deducted by the employer as the employee's premiums for the year` MINUS `B, the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted had the employer not made the excess payment`)
           LESS THAN `the amount that was deducted by the employer`
    THEN `A, the aggregate of all amounts deducted by the employer as the employee's premiums for the year` MINUS `B, the aggregate of all amounts that would have been deducted had the employer not made the excess payment`
    ELSE `the amount that was deducted by the employer`

§ `Section 82.1 - succession of employers`

-- src:1352 | 82.1 If, in a year after 2003, one employer immediately succeeds another as the employer of an employee as a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation or the acquisition — with the agreement of the former employer or by operation of law — of all or part of an undertaking or business of the former employer, the successor employer may, for the application of section 82, take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid under this Act by the former employer in respect of the year in relation to the employment of the employee as if they had been deducted, remitted or paid by the successor employer. If the employer takes those amounts into account with respect to the employer’s premium, the employer shall also take them into account with respect to the employee’s premium.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82.1 (src:1352)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `one employer immediately succeeds another as the employer of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by the formation or dissolution of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by the acquisition of all or part of an undertaking or business of the former employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquisition was with the agreement of the former employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquisition was by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` IF
        year GREATER THAN 2003
    AND `one employer immediately succeeds another as the employer of an employee`
    AND (   `by the formation or dissolution of a corporation`
         OR (`by the acquisition of all or part of an undertaking or business of the former employer`
             AND (`the acquisition was with the agreement of the former employer` OR `the acquisition was by operation of law`)))

-- "If the employer takes those amounts into account with respect to the employer's premium, the employer shall also take
-- them into account with respect to the employee's premium."
-- src:1352 | 82.1 If, in a year after 2003, one employer immediately succeeds another as the employer of an employee as a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation or the acquisition — with the agreement of the former employer or by operation of law — of all or part of an undertaking or business of the former employer, the successor employer may, for the application of section 82, take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid under this Act by the former employer in respect of the year in relation to the employment of the employee as if they had been deducted, remitted or paid by the successor employer. If the employer takes those amounts into account with respect to the employer’s premium, the employer shall also take them into account with respect to the employee’s premium.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 82.1 (src:1352)
GIVEN `the successor employer takes those amounts into account with respect to the employer's premium` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82.1 the successor employer shall also take them into account with respect to the employee's premium` IF
    `the successor employer takes those amounts into account with respect to the employer's premium`

§ `Section 83 - liability of directors`

-- src:1354 | 83 (1) If an employer who fails to deduct or remit an amount as and when required under subsection 82(1) is a corporation, the persons who were the directors of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable, together with the corporation, to pay Her Majesty that amount and any related interest or penalties.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 83(1) (src:1354)
GIVEN `the employer is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer failed to deduct or remit an amount as and when required under subsection 82(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 83(1) the person is jointly and severally liable with the corporation` IF
        `the employer is a corporation`
    AND `the employer failed to deduct or remit an amount as and when required under subsection 82(1)`
    AND `the person was a director of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred`

-- "That amount and any related interest or penalties."
-- src:1354 | 83 (1) If an employer who fails to deduct or remit an amount as and when required under subsection 82(1) is a corporation, the persons who were the directors of the corporation at the time when the failure occurred are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable, together with the corporation, to pay Her Majesty that amount and any related interest or penalties.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 83(1) (src:1354)
GIVEN `the amount the corporation failed to deduct or remit` IS A NUMBER
      `any related interest` IS A NUMBER
      `any related penalties` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 83(1) the amount for which the directors are liable together with the corporation` IS
    `the amount the corporation failed to deduct or remit` PLUS `any related interest` PLUS `any related penalties`

-- Subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act (not deposited) "apply, with such modifications as the circumstances
-- require, to a director of the corporation".
-- src:1356 | (2) Subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a director of the corporation.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 83(2) (src:1356)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 83(2) subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act apply to the person` IF
    `the person is a director of the corporation`

-- src:1358 | (3) The provisions of this Part respecting the assessment of an employer for an amount payable under this Act and respecting the rights and obligations of an employer so assessed apply to a director of the corporation in respect of an amount payable by the director under subsection (1) in the same manner and to the same extent as if the director were the employer mentioned in those provisions.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 83(3) (src:1358)
GIVEN `the person is liable as a director under subsection 83(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 83(3) the assessment provisions of this Part apply to the person as if they were the employer` IF
    `the person is liable as a director under subsection 83(1)`

§ `Section 84 - the employer's premium is not recoverable from the insured person`

-- "Despite any contract to the contrary": no input about a contract, because none changes the answer. The section speaks of
-- the employer's premium only; for any other amount it says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1360 | 84 Despite any contract to the contrary, an employer is not entitled to recover from an insured person the employer’s premium payable by the employer either by withholding the amount of the premium from the person’s wages or otherwise.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 84 (src:1360)
GIVEN `the amount is the employer's premium payable by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 84 the employer is entitled to recover the amount from the person` IS
    IF `the amount is the employer's premium payable by the employer` AND `the person is an insured person`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
